title: "Not a wrapper — what is deterministic, what the model decides, what is verified"
---
flowchart LR

    A["<b>1 · DETERMINISTIC</b><br/><i>no model, no tokens,<br/>no chance of being wrong</i><br/><br/>• PDF text layer + per-block<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;coordinates (PyMuPDF)<br/>• BM25 over the manual's own<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;printed headings<br/>• SPEC PATH: a torque question<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;answers from parsed rows —<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>0 LLM calls, $0.00013</b><br/>• PARTS CATALOG: 295 taxonomy<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;entries matched to the manual's<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;own words — <b>0 LLM calls</b><br/>• answer cache · currency maths ·<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;URL liveness · highlight geometry"]

    B["<b>2 · THE MODEL ONLY EVER<br/>DECIDES THREE THINGS</b><br/><br/>• <b>WHICH VEHICLE</b> is in this photo<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;— and only from our catalog<br/><br/>• <b>WHICH PAGE IDs</b> answer this<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;sentence — it returns ids,<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;never a word of prose<br/><br/>• <b>HOW TO SAY</b> what those pages<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;already print — chat, the one<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;place words are generated"]

    C["<b>3 · VERIFIED IN CODE BEFORE<br/>ANYTHING IS SHOWN</b><br/><br/>• every ingest quote must be found<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;in the PDF text layer, or dropped<br/>• every picked id must be in the<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;candidate list, or dropped<br/>• every citation quote is sliced by<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;the SERVER out of the original<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;page — verbatim by construction,<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;not by trusting the model<br/>• every number must be printed on a<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;page the model was given<br/>• every offer URL is fetched<br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;before it ships"]

    D["<b>WHAT THE MECHANIC SEES</b><br/><br/>the manufacturer's own page,<br/>with the lines marked.<br/><br/><b>Never AI prose presented<br/>as the answer.</b><br/><br/>Measured: 100% top-1 over<br/>150 queries · 100% valid citations<br/>0 invented numbers · 0 dealer referrals<br/><b>$0.00038 per ask · $0.10 per manual</b>"]

    A ==> B ==> C ==> D

